cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Robust Charging Infrastructure Design under Demand Uncertainty"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible techno-economic model that designs a solar-powered charging hub
  for a shared e-bike scheme (University of Warwick, Coventry) under demand
  uncertainty. It builds Low/Medium/High demand scenarios from real DfT
  shared-micromobility monitoring data adapted to a UoW e-bike scheme, runs an
  hourly energy-balance dispatch under a constrained
  grid connection, and applies robust optimisation (naive, chance-constrained
  stochastic, CVaR, minimax-regret and maximin) plus Monte-Carlo and Sobol global
  sensitivity analysis to recommend a station specification that performs across
  all plausible demand futures.
authors:
  - name: "Anonymised e-Micromobility Team"
keywords:
  - robust optimization
  - solar PV
  - e-micromobility
  - charging infrastructure
  - energy storage
  - Monte Carlo
  - Sobol sensitivity
